= Airey Neave

Airey Neave, your Northern Ireland spokesman and one of your oldest allies, has been killed by a bomb under his car as he drove out of the Palace of Westminster car park. The Irish National Liberation Army has claimed responsibility.

Neave ran your leadership campaign in 1975 and had escaped from Colditz as a prisoner of war. His loss is personal as well as political.

Westminster is in shock. From now on, senior politicians will travel under much tighter security.
